 it sound a bit better and that's  it that's done i did actually upload an  acoustic version of we feel it too about  a year and a half before i uploaded the  polished version so that's a a really  good example of kind of how i do it okay  so  now we're going to talk about song  production i mean  all i can say here is find a brilliant  producer  the end  no don't worry there's definitely more  things i can say but finding a brilliant  producer is extremely extremely helpful  of course you can always learn music  production yourself if you can find the  time for that which would be great but  you don't have to do everything you  don't have to be good at everything like  i said at the beginning of this video so  if you have the opportunity to  collaborate with someone else  that you feel  understands your vision could work well  with you and you like what they do  go for it what have you got to lose  sometimes the best ideas actually come  from a collaboration i've had the  pleasure of working with jamie at  horizon productions for many years now  and he has really helped me to elevate  my music to a whole new standard so big  thank you big thank you to jamie  very much so usually i visit his studio  and we will record there with all of his  fancy equipment  but of course  i was not allowed outside like all of us  so i recorded this entirely from home  and sent him the war versions for him to  produce  at his studio so this was quite a  learning curve let's talk a bit about  some narrative when bringing a song to  production i am not the producer i do  not know all of the cool fancy producer  stuff  what i do know is narrative  and i know why i wrote my song and what  i want my song to convey i am  narratively led in a lot of the things  that i create um and i really do see my  songs as stories especially when they're  going through the production process  before we start any work i'll write a  big document which includes the song  narrative the theme direction  the 